<https://ontology.pointonezero.com/strategy/apqc/utilities> a owl:Ontology ;
    dct:title "P1Z Industry Overlay: APQC Utilities PCF" ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.1.0" ;
    dct:source "APQC Process Classification Framework (PCF), Utilities, Excel Version 8.0" ;
    dct:description "Utilities industry overlay module: a separate module importing the cross-industry spine (PCF v8.0, spine v0.3.0, core v0.4.0). Adds and specializes only, never redefines a core or spine term: industry-new process elements (with parentProcess links into the spine or this overlay) and industry-new metrics with their cross-maps. Shared elements and metrics remain asserted solely by the spine and cross-industry metrics files. Version-skew editorial differences observed in the industry workbook (label case changes, metric text polish, coarser metric placements) are deliberately not asserted; the cross-industry v8.0 files are canonical for shared content." ;
    dct:rights "APQC Process Classification Framework (PCF) is an open standard developed by APQC, a nonprofit that promotes benchmarking and best practices worldwide. The PCF is intended to facilitate organizational improvement through process management and benchmarking, regardless of industry, size, or geography. To download the full PCF or industry-specific versions of the PCF, as well as associated measures and benchmarking, please visit www.apqc.org/pcf." .

# Industry-new process elements (135, levels 1-4)

apqc:PCF16791 a p1z:Process ;
    skos:prefLabel "Evaluate IP acquisition options - external IP licensing" ;
    p1z:apqcId "16791" ;
    p1z:apqcHierarchyId "1.1.1.11" ;
    p1z:apqcLevel 4 ;
    p1z:metricsAvailable false ;
    skos:definition "Establishing and defining measures and methods for valuation and acquisitions of IP. Defining the value of intellectual property for buying and licensing of IP rights." ;
    p1z:parentProcess apqc:PCF10017 .

apqc:PCF19126 a p1z:FunctionalDomain ;
    skos:prefLabel "Develop tariffs and service charges for regulated products and services" ;
    p1z:apqcId "19126" ;
    p1z:apqcHierarchyId "2.4" ;
    p1z:apqcLevel 2 ;
    p1z:metricsAvailable false ;
    skos:definition "Assigning tariffs to electricity, gas, or water supplied by a utility through a utility network to its customer. Tariffs also recover the costs of generation, storage, delivering to customers, collection and treatment, as well as billing and collection. Obtaining regulatory approval for a tariff in a regulated market is only done once.  Utility cannot change the price without regulatory approval. The tariff structure is submitted to regulator with a justification.   In competitive markets, pricing of the electricity, gas and/or water commodities is subject to business discretion and may be adjusted many times.   In deregulated markets, the use-of-system charges are still regulated, while generation, wholesale and retail energy charges are not." ;
    p1z:parentProcess apqc:PCF10003 .

